---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{% set current = cv.roles[0] %}

{# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Hero -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule">
  <div class="u-shell grid items-end gap-12 py-16 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_16rem] lg:py-24">
    <div>
      <h1 class="u-display text-hero">Florian<br />Zeba<span class="text-ultra">.</span></h1>

      <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-[1.12rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2 sm:text-[1.22rem]">
        I design the platforms enterprises run their data on, and I still write the pipelines
        that fill them. An architecture is only as good as the thing you can
        <em class="font-display not-italic text-ink">point at when a number is wrong</em>.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-3">
        {{ current.role }} at {{ current.org }}. Previously CANCOM, SOFTWERK and PwC,
        alongside my own practice.
      </p>

      <p class="u-meta mt-4">{{ cv.location }} — enterprise data platforms, applied AI</p>

      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="/consulting/" class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 bg-ink px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.76rem] uppercase tracking-[0.09em] text-surface transition-colors hover:bg-ultra">
          Work with me
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/research/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 border border-rule bg-surface px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.76rem] uppercase tracking-[0.09em] text-ink-2 transition-colors hover:border-ink hover:text-ink">
          Research
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="hidden lg:block">
      <img src="/assets/profile.webp" alt="Portrait of Florian Zeba" width="440" height="560" class="w-full grayscale-[0.18] contrast-[1.02]" fetchpriority="high" />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{# --------------------------------------------------------- Credentials -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule bg-surface-2/40 py-10">
  <div class="u-shell flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-x-10 gap-y-6">
    <div>
      <p class="u-eyebrow text-[0.64rem]">Qualifications</p>
      <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-[0.82rem] text-ink-2">{{ cv.credentials | join(" · ") }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-10 gap-y-4">
      {% set m = { label: "Articles published", value: collections.posts.length, source: "This site, " + build.year } %}
      {% include "partials/metric.njk" %}
      {% set m = { label: "Years in data & AI", value: cv.since | yearsSince, source: "Earliest role listed on the CV" } %}
      {% include "partials/metric.njk" %}
      {% set m = { label: "Certifications", value: cv.certifications.length, source: "KNIME, Bloomberg, Alteryx, Qlik" } %}
      {% include "partials/metric.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------- Career -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="u-shell u-manuscript">
    <p class="u-eyebrow lg:pt-1.5">Career</p>
    <div>
      <h2 class="u-display mb-3 max-w-2xl text-section">Consulting and building, at the same time — not in sequence.</h2>
      <p class="mb-9 max-w-2xl text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
        A CV flattens a career into a list, which hides the part that matters. The consultancy
        roles, the engineering work and my own practice were not phases. They ran together —
        FZEBA.com has been open alongside every employed role since February 2025.
      </p>
      {% set timelineNote = "FZEBA.com has run alongside every employed role since 2025." %}
      {% include "partials/timeline.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Orgs -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="u-shell u-manuscript">
    <p class="u-eyebrow lg:pt-1.5">Organisations</p>
    <div>
      <h2 class="u-display mb-3 max-w-2xl text-section">Where the work was done.</h2>
      <p class="mb-9 max-w-2xl text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
        The chart above names them; this says what they are. Each row states the actual
        relationship — payroll, advisory, or a company of my own.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-px">
        {% for o in orgs %}{% include "partials/org-row.njk" %}{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------ Projects -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule bg-surface-2/40 py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="u-shell u-manuscript">
    <p class="u-eyebrow lg:pt-1.5">Projects</p>
    <div>
      <h2 class="u-display mb-3 max-w-2xl text-section">Things I built and shipped.</h2>
      <p class="mb-9 max-w-2xl text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
        Client work, written up. Each one names the problem, the stack and what actually
        changed once it ran.
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-px">
        {% for project in collections.projects %}
          {% set rowIndex = loop.index %}
          {% include "partials/numbered-row.njk" %}
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href="/projects/" class="u-link inline-block py-1 font-mono text-[0.76rem] uppercase tracking-[0.09em]">All projects →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------ Research -- #}
{% set paper = research.papers[0] %}
<section class="border-b border-rule py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="u-shell u-manuscript">
    <p class="u-eyebrow lg:pt-1.5">Research</p>
    <div>
      <h2 class="u-display mb-3 max-w-2xl text-section">Governance you can prove, not guardrails you hope hold.</h2>
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
        {{ paper.title }} — co-authored with Marius-Constantin Dinu at {{ paper.affiliation }}.
        It treats an agent's validate–repair loop as a monotone operator on a lattice of
        satisfied requirements, so “done” becomes a least fixed point you can prove rather
        than a heuristic stopping rule.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-10 gap-y-4">
        {% for m in paper.metrics %}{% include "partials/metric.njk" %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href="/research/" class="u-link inline-block py-1 font-mono text-[0.76rem] uppercase tracking-[0.09em]">Papers and applied work →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------- Writing -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="u-shell u-manuscript">
    <p class="u-eyebrow lg:pt-1.5">Writing</p>
    <div>
      <div class="mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4">
        {# No count in the heading: it reads as a claim and goes stale the
           moment a post is added. The live figure lives on /posts/. #}
        <h2 class="u-display max-w-2xl text-section">Notes on making data trustworthy.</h2>
        <a href="/posts/" class="u-link inline-block py-1 font-mono text-[0.76rem] uppercase tracking-[0.09em]">All posts →</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="border-t border-rule">
        {% for post in collections.posts | head(6) %}
          {% include "partials/post-row.njk" %}
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------- Contact -- #}
<section class="border-b border-rule bg-ink py-16 text-surface sm:py-20">
  <div class="u-shell">
    <p class="u-eyebrow !text-surface/45">Get in touch</p>
    <h2 class="u-display mt-4 max-w-3xl text-[clamp(1.7rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
      Looking for someone to design the platform <span class="text-surface/50">and</span> still write the pipeline?
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-3">
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.author.email }}" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 border border-surface bg-surface px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.76rem] uppercase tracking-[0.09em] text-ink transition-opacity hover:opacity-85">
        {{ site.author.email }}
      </a>
      {% for s in site.social %}
        <a href="{{ s.url }}" rel="me noopener" class="inline-block py-1 font-mono text-[0.78rem] text-surface/75 underline decoration-surface/30 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-surface">{{ s.name }} ↗</a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
